<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring wheat bids fall.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring wheat bids fall.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring wheat cash bids were lower in the northern Plains cash markets largely in reaction to sharply lower Minneapolis spring wheat futures, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Wheat sales were light as farmers continued to concentrate on planting spring wheat. Serious infestations of wild oats forced plowing and replanting of spring wheat fields in north central Montana. Dealers there said spring rain diluted herbicides, allowing the oats to infest the fields.</p>
<p>Planting continued in the Red River Valley in eastern North Dakota and western Minnesota.  </p>
